All 5 additions are the conditional theme-colour skip named in the standing
rules ("every conditional theme-colour t.Skip"): they fire only when a
specific themes package palette happens to assign the same colour to a key
token and a hint token, in which case the distinctness assertion the test
is checking would be vacuously true rather than a real check, so the test
skips itself rather than passing for the wrong reason. No other t.Skip was
added in range (confirmed features/i1_repro_test.go, the pre-existing
opt-in TestI1KeystrokeDropReproduction driver, is untouched by this diff
range: git diff 1cfbd5a..HEAD -- features/i1_repro_test.go is empty).
